@nsobid-28C4287AEE36F7499DA60F3E68B54C70DA382D75

# Splatoon 3 11.3.0 - Disable FXAA

@flag print_values
@flag offset_shift 0x100

// Disables the FXAA post-process anti-aliasing pass in agl::pfx::FilterAA::draw
// (sub_71047069D0). The filter dispatches on its antialias_type field
// (this+0x730) through a 4-entry jump table: 0 = FXAA, 1 = ReduceAA ("reduce"),
// 2 = SMAA (sub_710470A690), 3 = user callback (this+0xA10). The constructor
// (sub_71047026F0) leaves antialias_type = 0 and enable (this+0x750) = 1, so
// FXAA is the live path on a stock game.
//
// When enable is 0 the function already falls through to a plain
// ImageFilter2D::drawTexture pass-through copy at 0x7104706C1C -- the exact
// "no AA" output we want. This replaces the FXAA case's first instruction with
// an unconditional branch to that block, so only FXAA is redirected;
// ReduceAA and SMAA stay intact if a scene ever selects them. Because it
// patches code rather than a config default, no env/byaml archive can undo it.

@enabled
04706B04 46000014   // B (pass-through)   (was LDR S0,[X23,#0x988] = FXAA case entry)
@stop

// Offsets reverse-engineered against Splatoon 3's sead + Cmn/spl::gfx + agl/gsys
// engine. 11.3.0 retail is symbol-stripped -- every site above was located by
// structure and byte-verified against the IDB before being written.
//
// https://github.com/RAMDRAGONS/switch-patches
